This is a placeholder, not a valid Mosquitto password file.
Create it before starting the stack:

  docker run --rm -it -v "$PWD/mosquitto/config:/mosquitto/config" eclipse-mosquitto:2 \
    mosquitto_passwd -c /mosquitto/config/passwords iot_device

Then add a separate user for Node-RED (recommended):

  docker run --rm -it -v "$PWD/mosquitto/config:/mosquitto/config" eclipse-mosquitto:2 \
    mosquitto_passwd /mosquitto/config/passwords nodered

Use the prompts to set passwords. Do not commit the generated password file.
For a quick isolated local test only, you can temporarily use allow_anonymous true,
but do not expose port 1883 to the internet.
